00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.389 align:start position:0%
 
i've been reviewing apple's ipad pro  ever since their controversial  what's a computer ad in 2017 which  basically sparked years of  disappointment  in the ipad pro's very limiting software  especially after the 2018 ipad pro got a  massive redesign  and an extremely powerful a12x chip and  in my review of that 11 inch ipad pro  over two and a half years ago  i said these words apple may continue  adding computer-like features here and  there but the ipad pro will never be a  true laptop replacement  until apple wants it to be and now here  we are in 2021  with the m1 ipad pro that we've had our  hands on for the past three weeks  and the story's basically the same the  performance of this new ipad pro  is absolutely mind-boggling especially  when you compare it to the very best  tablets on the market  they literally don't stand a chance and  they won't  for years but the problem comes when the  ipad os software is so  limited that you literally cannot take  advantage of  all of that performance and with the  newly released ipad os 15  people are so upset and disappointed  that they are literally  returning their new m1 ipad pros  because apple didn't add the  computer-like features  that everyone was waiting for and in my  personal opinion  i think a lot of people are overreacting  at least for the 11 inch ipad pro which  i'm reviewing in  this video and i'll explain my reasoning  in just a minute but first i want to  talk about  why people are so upset and to be honest  it's kind of apple's fault they  basically baited everyone into having  massive expectations for ipad os 15  by first of all putting the exact same  chip  from the incredible new m1 max into the  ipad pro  as well as allowing you to get up to 16  gigabytes of ram  which was unheard of on an ipad pro  since the previous model  only had 6 gigs and as we all recently  found out  the previous ipad os 14 software  wouldn't even allow apps to use  more than 5 gigabytes of that 16 gig  limit on the new ipad pro  and we proved this in our 8 gigabyte  versus 16 gig  ipad pro comparison video where there  were basically  no differences in the worst part is that  the previous a12z ipad pro  was still overpowered for ipad os 14.  so the fact that apple gave the new  model the m1 chip  with up to 16 gigs of ram basically  baited everyone into thinking that apple  was gonna finally turn  the ipad pro into a real computer  replacement  by removing artificial software  limitations and adding pro apps like  final cut and logic  but of course that didn't happen so  here's the main question we need to  answer  why did apple still end up putting the  crazy m1 chip  into the ipad pro if they didn't have  plans to completely  revolutionize the software well first of  all  not everyone realizes this but the a12z  chip from the previous ipad pro  had almost the same exact chip layout as  the m1  four performance cores four efficiency  cores  eight graphics cores and a neural engine  so in reality  the m1 chip isn't that groundbreaking or  special  it's basically just a new version of the  a12z  except that it's built on tsmc's more  efficient five nanometer  transistors instead of the old seven  nanometer ones  so if you think about it apple could  have easily gone with their previous  trend  and named the chip the a14x like  everyone is expecting them to  and we even expected the a14x and the m1  to have basically the same performance  since they would have had  the same layout essentially the same  chip so here's the real question that we  have to answer  why did apple choose to ditch the a14x  trend  and literally just take the m1 chip out  of the mac  and throw it into the ipad pro well it  actually makes much more sense than you  think  at least for apple first of all the m1  chip is basically the mascot or the  symbol of the apple silicon transition  since they've literally packed that chip  into half of their entire mac lineup so  apple's goal  is to essentially make the m1 chip go  viral so that their apple silicon  transition goes viral  and what better way to do that is to  stick the m1 and yet another popular  apple product  reason number two is that the m1 chip  carries an outstanding reputation  among the mac crowd for being incredibly  powerful  while using very little power so having  that chip  in the ipad pro makes it seem a whole  lot more pro  than ever before reason number three is  that since the m1 chip already comes  with a thunderbolt  controller built in it automatically  added support  for the ipad pro's new thunderbolt port  yet again  making it seem much more pro and reason  number four is that believe it or not  the m1 chip is actually much cheaper per  unit  than if apple made a slightly different  a14x chip  just for the ipad pro because the m1 is  literally the only option for the new  macbook air  macbook pro mac mini 24 inch imac  and the ipad pro apple can mass  manufacture that one chip  and save a ton of cash compared to if  they made a specific chip  just for the ipad pro which would take a  lot of extra r d  so basically putting the m1 chip in this  ipad  made absolutely the most financial sense  for apple  but the problem is that it caused  extremely high  expectations and a lot of people were  let down  even to the point of returning their  ipad pros  and don't get me wrong i'm not blaming  you for having huge  expectations because apple kind of put  themselves in a box  and if you want to find out how apple  did that click the subscribe button  below  because max is gonna go in depth with  apple's dilemma  and his 12.9 inch m1 ipad pro review  going up tomorrow but for this review  i'm gonna look at the 11 inch model  for what it truly is the truth is that  the 11 inch m1 ipad pro for 800  is a much better value than the previous  ipad pro  which we already were recommending  because of its exclusive features  compared to the lower end ipads in fact  we still recommended the a12z ipad pro  when the brand new 600 ipad air 4 came  out late last year  because in reality you truly did get a  lot for the extra 200  but now with the m1 ipad pro the list of  advantages over the air is so  huge that we literally told people not  to buy the ipad air  in our recent ipad buyers guide video  because at 600  it's simply too expensive for what you  get compared to spending  two hundred dollars more for the m1 pro  for example  the pro gets a 120 hertz pro motion  display  with 600 nits of brightness instead of  500  which allows it to support hdr video it  also gets  extra camera features including an  ultrawide camera on the back  a flash a lidar scanner for 3d modeling  and a much better 12 megapixel ultrawide  selfie camera  with the new center stage feature it  gets much better quad stereo speakers  instead of dual stereo on the air  it gets much better studio quality  microphones it gets optional 5g  connectivity  it gets the thunderbolt port compared to  a pretty limited  usb c port it gets much faster ssd  write speeds it gets 8 gigs of ram  instead of 4 on the air  it gets 128 gigs of storage instead of  64  and of course it gets the m1 chip  compared to the a14  on the air and taking a look at all of  the benchmarks that we ran  it's faster in everything including the  single core performance  which gives it a snappier web browsing  experience  it's also much faster in terms of  multi-core performance  and it was over twice as fast in terms  of real-world  graphics performance as well so the  point that i'm trying to make  is that if you get rid of all of those  high expectations  and just look at the m1 ipad pro  compared to the last one  it's definitely a nice improvement the  11 inch ipad pro is now further cemented  as the best tablet ever made with  performance that'll run even the best  apps that will be available  years from now and incredibly high  quality speakers and microphones  and the killer 120hz display even  without the mini led tech  and it's got the best stylus experience  you can get  with the apple pencil and the software  works  incredibly well even if it doesn't come  with the macbook replacing features  that we were all hoping for so i've  gotta say that this is one of the best  times to buy an ipad pro  because we've basically just reached the  peak of ipad hardware  and if by some chance apple decides to  fix the software issues  within the next couple of years or even  the next few years  the m1 ipad pro will be ready for it and  the reason i say it's reached peak  hardware is because the m1 chip is so  powerful  that it's hitting the limits of the thin  ipad pro's  passive cooling system so when the next  ipad pro comes out  probably in the fall of 2022 it'll  likely get the m2 chip  which honestly won't be that big of an  improvement and as far as everything  else like the design  face id all of the cameras the speakers  the microphones the thunderbolt port the  keyboard  case support with the smart connector  all of the magnets  and everything else that has to do with  hardware they've basically all reached  their peak and they make using the ipad  pro as a tablet  the best experience out there in terms  of everything from media consumption  note-taking drawing gaming and common  computer use  the only issue is that the 2018 ipad pro  was so far ahead of its time that even  today  it checks all of those boxes not quite  as well as the new m1 model  but it still does so if you own a 2018  or 2020 ipad pro  don't bother upgrading unless you're  doing something specific  that you think would make a big  difference for you on the new m1 ipad  pro  like for example high end gaming since  the m1 chip stays incredibly cool  compared to the a12 z chip which  overheats  like crazy and gentian impact or maybe  you want to take advantage of the  thunderbolt porn  like how we were able to hook up this  owc thunderbolt dock  meant for m1 max which basically turns  one thunderbolt port into  three and as you can see it actually  works great on the new ipad pro  but other than those couple of  improvements the new m1 ipad pro  isn't really that groundbreaking or  different  compared to the 2018 and 2020 models and  with that said there is actually one  piece of hardware on the 11 inch m1 ipad  pro  that hasn't yet reached its peak and  that is of course  the regular lcd display compared to the  12.9 inch model's mini led  and in my personal opinion i think apple  is going to give  that new display to the 11 ipad pro next  year  so they'll have a good excuse to bump up  the base price by 100 bucks  to 900 for the base model so if you  don't already have a 2018 or newer ipad  pro  and you're thinking of buying the new m1  you basically have  two options you can wait a full year and  a half with the hopes of getting that  mini led display  on the 11 inch model for probably nine  hundred dollars  or you can buy the current model right  now for 800 bucks  and enjoy it for the entire time that  you would have otherwise been waiting  but either way the m1 ipad pro is  definitely the best tablet in the world  with hardware that's so good that it's  basically future proof  so if apple ever does fix the software  and make it more of a laptop replacement  you'll be ready for it but as it stands  today ipad os 15 is extremely  disappointing compared to how good the  ipad pro's hardware  is and that's exactly what max is going  to talk about  and his review of the 12.9 inch mini led  model  so if you're not already subscribed  click that circle above so you don't  miss out on his review  so thanks for watching and we'll see you  in tomorrow's video

